\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Hills of the North, rejoice,
\par Hark to the advent voice,
\par Valley and lowland, sing:
\par Though absent long, your Lord is nigh;
\par He judgement brings and victory.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Isles of the Soutern seas,
\par Deep in your coral caves
\par Pent be each warring breeze, 
\par Lulled be your restless waves:
\par He comes to reign with boundless sway,
\par And make your wastes His great highway.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Lands of the East, awake,
\par Soon shall your sons be free;
\par And rise to liberty:
\par On your far hills, long cold and grey,
\par Has dwed the everlasting day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Shores of the utmost West,
\par Ye that have waited long, 
\par Unvisited, unblest,
\par Break forth to swelling song:
\par High raise the note, that Jesus died,
\par Yet lives and riegns-the Crucified!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Shout while ye journey home,
\par Songs be in every mouth;
\par Lo! from the North we come, 
\par From East, and West, and South.
\par Citiy of God, the bond are free;
\par We come to live and reign in thee.
\par 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

